---
source: crates/aozora-cli/tests/snapshot_cli.rs
expression: "run(&[\"tui\", \"--help\"])"
---
Open a full-screen editor with source, preview, and diagnostic panes. Preview HTML, nodes, or Pandoc
through the document subcommands' engine. Edits refresh all panes after a debounce delay, providing
an alternative to `--watch`. `Ctrl-S` saves, `Ctrl-L` cycles language, `Ctrl-P` cycles preview, and
`Ctrl-Q` quits. Supply `[FILE]` to open a document

Usage: aozora tui [OPTIONS] [FILE]

Arguments:
  [FILE]
          Open this file in the editor. Omit to start with an empty buffer, where `Ctrl-S` reports
          that no file is available

Options:
      --preview <PREVIEW>
          Choose the initial preview: `html`, `nodes`, or `pandoc`. Defaults to HTML, matching
          `aozora render`. The other views match `aozora inspect nodes` and `aozora pandoc`. Cycle
          views with `Ctrl-P`

          Possible values:
          - html:   Render HTML as `aozora render` does
          - nodes:  Show source nodes as JSON, matching `aozora inspect nodes`
          - pandoc: Show the Pandoc abstract syntax tree as formatted JSON, matching `aozora pandoc`

          [default: html]

  -E, --encoding <ENCODING>
          Choose the source encoding for `[FILE]`: `auto`, `utf8`, or `sjis`. Defaults to `auto`.
          The Unicode edit buffer always saves as UTF-8 with `Ctrl-S`

          Possible values:
          - auto: Detect the source encoding. Read valid UTF-8 directly and decode other input as
            Shift_JIS
          - utf8: Force UTF-8 and report an error for invalid input
          - sjis: Force Shift_JIS decoding

          [default: auto]

      --color <WHEN>
          Choose `auto`, `always`, or `never` for diagnostic color. `auto` uses terminal detection
          and honours `NO_COLOR`, `CLICOLOR`, and `CLICOLOR_FORCE`. Defaults to `.aozora.toml`'s
          `color`, then `auto`. Applies to graphical diagnostics and `fmt --diff`. `spec kinds`
          tables stay monochrome. Accepts placement after any subcommand

          Possible values:
          - auto:   Use color when stdout is a terminal, honoring `NO_COLOR`, `CLICOLOR`, and
            `CLICOLOR_FORCE`
          - always: Always use color, even when piped
          - never:  Never use color

  -v, --verbose...
          Increase stderr log verbosity with `-v` for info, `-vv` for debug, or `-vvv` for trace.
          Preserves stdout and diagnostic output. `AOZORA_LOG` overrides this setting. One `-v`
          cancels `--quiet`. Accepts placement after any subcommand

  -q, --quiet
          Restrict stderr logging to errors. Preserves stdout. One `-v` cancels this setting.
          `AOZORA_LOG` overrides it. Accepts placement after any subcommand

      --lang <LOCALE>
          Choose the human message language with a `BCP-47` tag: `en`, `ja`, or `zh`. Applies to the
          stdin guard, watch banner, and `explain`. Resolves through `--lang > AOZORA_LANG >
          .aozora.toml lang > LANG`, then English. Unknown locales use English. Preserves JSON,
          short diagnostics, codes, exit status, schemas, and source encoding. Accepts placement
          after any subcommand

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version

Examples:
  aozora tui                     # start with an empty buffer
  aozora tui hon.aozora          # open a file to edit
  aozora tui --preview nodes     # start the preview pane in nodes view
  aozora tui -E sjis book.txt    # decode a Shift_JIS file on open

Keys (while running):
  Ctrl-S  save the buffer to the file      Ctrl-L  cycle message language
  Ctrl-P  cycle the preview view           Ctrl-Q  quit
Every unmodified keystroke edits the source pane; the preview and diagnostics
panes refresh automatically, debounced.
